  {
    title: "Henry Santana: Why We Need to End Parking Minimums",
    description:
      "A deep dive on how parking requirements impact the housing crisis in Boston.",
    type: "article",
    url: "https://mailchi.mp/boston/2025-12-parking-minimums/",
    iconPath:
      "M14 2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v16a2 2 0 002 2h12a2 2 0 002-2V8l-6-6z M14 2v6h6 M10 9h4 M10 13h4 M10 17h4",
  },
  {
    title: "Vox: The High Cost of Free Parking",
    description:
      "A video breaking down the impact free parking has on cities and the research of Donald Shoup.",
    type: "video",
    url: "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Akm7ik-H_7U",
    iconPath:
      "M14.752 11.168l-3.197-2.132A1 1 0 0010 9.87v4.263a1 1 0 001.555.832l3.197-2.132a1 1 0 000-1.664z M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z",
  },
  {
    title: "Planetizen: Parking Reform Can Boost Homebuilding 40 to 70 Percent",
    description:
      "An article examining the evidence that parking flexibility is key to housing abundance.",
    type: "article",
    url: "https://www.planetizen.com/news/2024/12/133177-parking-reform-can-boost-homebuilding-40-70-percent",
    iconPath:
      "M14 2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v16a2 2 0 002 2h12a2 2 0 002-2V8l-6-6z M14 2v6h6 M10 9h4 M10 13h4 M10 17h4",
  },
  {
    title:
      "Sightline Institute: Parking Reform Legalized Most of the New Homes in Buffalo and Seattle",
    description:
      "A case study on how changing parking policies led to increased housing development in two U.S. cities.",
    type: "article",
    url: "https://www.sightline.org/2023/04/13/parking-reform-legalized-most-of-the-new-homes-in-buffalo-and-seattle",
    iconPath:
      "M14 2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v16a2 2 0 002 2h12a2 2 0 002-2V8l-6-6z M14 2v6h6 M10 9h4 M10 13h4 M10 17h4",
  },
];
---

<section id="benefits" class="bg-white text-gray-800">
  <div class="container mx-auto py-16 md:py-24 px-4">
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-center mb-12">
      How Will This Benefit Boston?
    </h2>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Benefit 1 -->
      <div
        class="emoji-animation-container bg-gray-50 p-8 rounded-lg shadow-sm text-center
      transition-all duration-300 hover:ring-4 hover:ring-blue-500 hover:ring-opacity-75"
      >
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 text-gray-900">
          More Affordable Housing
        </h3>
        <p class="text-gray-600">
          "From an affordability and access perspective, larger parking minimums
          force buyers and renters to pay for parking spaces they may not want
          or need, which could cause would-be buyers and renters to be unable to
          afford to live in a particular area. Parking mandates can also
          decrease the number of housing units in a development, thereby
          reducing access through fewer units."
        </p>
        <footer class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500">
          — <a
            href="https://www.housingaffordabilityinstitute.org/policy-center/parking-mandates/"
            class="underline hover:text-gray-700"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Housing Affordability Institute, "Affordability Roadblocks - Parking
            Mandates"
          </a>
        </footer>
        <span class="emoji-particle emoji-left">💰</span>
        <span class="emoji-particle emoji-right">📉</span>
      </div>

      <!-- Benefit 2 -->
      <div
        class="emoji-animation-container bg-gray-50 p-8 rounded-lg shadow-sm text-center
        transition-all duration-300 hover:ring-4 hover:ring-indigo-500 hover:ring-opacity-75"
      >
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 text-gray-900">
          Vibrant, Walkable Neighborhoods
        </h3>
        <p class="text-gray-600">
          "In Amsterdam, some street parking has become urban forest; in Paris,
          entire blocks outside schools have been repurposed as social spaces
          for kids. All that is possible in U.S. cities too. But first leaders
          must legalize the type of parking-lite, high-density housing that
          makes it possible for a neighborhood to be vibrant, walkable, and
          economically served by mass transit."
        </p>
        <footer class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500">
          — <a
            href="https://e360.yale.edu/features/free-parking-reform"
            class="underline hover:text-gray-700"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Henry Grabar, "How Parking Reform Is Helping Transform American
            Cities"
          </a>
        </footer>
        <span class="emoji-particle emoji-left">🚶‍➡️</span>
        <span class="emoji-particle emoji-right">🏙️</span>
      </div>

      <!-- Benefit 3 -->
      <div
        class="emoji-animation-container bg-gray-50 p-8 rounded-lg shadow-sm text-center
        transition-all duration-300 hover:ring-4 hover:ring-green-500 hover:ring-opacity-75"
      >
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 text-gray-900">
          A Greener, Healthier City
        </h3>

        <p class="text-gray-600">
          "Reducing the amount of parking in urban spaces can also greatly
          improve the quality of urban landscapes... lower automobile use per
          capita helps to reduce greenhouse gas emissions and pollution from
          cars around population centers. Additionally, decreasing the amount of
          built infrastructure like parking and roads can reduce the heat island
          effect."
        </p>
        <footer class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500">
          — <a
            href="https://www.eesi.org/articles/view/how-eliminating-parking-minimums-actually-makes-cities-better"
            class="underline hover:text-gray-700"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            EESI, "How Eliminating Parking Minimums Actually Makes Cities
            Better"
          </a>
        </footer>

        <!-- The Emojis! They are hidden by default via CSS -->
        <span class="emoji-particle emoji-left">🌳</span>
        <span class="emoji-particle emoji-right">🏃‍♀️</span>
        <!-- Added a different runner emoji for variety -->
      </div>
    </div>
    <!-- Resources Section -->
    <div class="border-gray-200 max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-16">
      <h3 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-center mb-12">
        Learn More
      </h3>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        {
          resources.map((resource) => (
            <a
              href={resource.url}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="bg-gray-50 hover:bg-gray-100 p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all duration-200 hover:scale-105 cursor-pointer block"
            >
              <div class="mb-4">
                <div class="inline-block p-2 bg-indigo-100 rounded-lg">
                  <svg
                    class="w-6 h-6 text-indigo-600"
                    fill="none"
                    stroke="currentColor"
                    stroke-width="1.5"
                    viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                  >
                    <path
                      stroke-linecap="round"
                      stroke-linejoin="round"
                      d={resource.iconPath}
                    />
                  </svg>
                </div>
                <span class="inline-block ml-3 text-xs font-semibold text-indigo-600 bg-indigo-50 px-2 py-1 rounded">
                  {resource.type === "article" && "Article"}
                  {resource.type === "video" && "Video"}
                  {resource.type === "book" && "Book"}
                  {resource.type === "website" && "Website"}
                </span>
              </div>
              <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">
                {resource.title}
              </h4>
              <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">{resource.description}</p>
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-20 pt-16 border-t border-gray-200"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* This is the custom CSS for the emoji animation.
      It's placed here in the <head> tag.
    */

  /* 1. The container needs 'position: relative' so we can
         position the emojis inside it.
      2. 'overflow: visible' is CRITICAL so the emojis
         can be seen when they move *outside* the card's box.
    */
  .emoji-animation-container {
    position: relative;
    overflow: visible;
    z-index: 10; /* Ensures emojis appear 'above' other cards */
  }

  /* 1. 'position: absolute' takes the emoji out of the normal flow.
      2. 'opacity: 0' makes it invisible by default.
      3. 'transition' animates the changes to opacity and position.
      4. 'pointer-events: none' is important so the emoji doesn't
         block your mouse from hovering on the card itself.
    */
  .emoji-particle {
    position: absolute;
    font-size: 2rem; /* Made emojis a bit bigger */
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    transition: all 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.175, 0.885, 0.32, 1.275); /* A 'bouncy' ease */
  }

  /* Positioning for the tree emoji */
  .emoji-left {
    top: 50%;
    left: 10%; /* Start slightly inside */
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  }

  /* Positioning for the runner emoji */
  .emoji-right {
    top: 50%;
    right: 10%; /* Start slightly inside */
    transform: translate(50%, -50%);
  }

  /* This is the 'hover' state.
      When the PARENT (.animated-card-container) is hovered...
      ...these styles apply to the child emoji elements.

      Also, only apply this on screens 768px wide and larger, to prevent issues on small screens.
    */
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .emoji-animation-container:hover .emoji-left {
      opacity: 1;
      left: -20%; /* Move it outside the card to the left */
      transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(-15deg); /* Add a tilt */
    }

    .emoji-animation-container:hover .emoji-right {
      opacity: 1;
      right: -20%; /* Move it outside the card to the right */
      transform: translate(50%, -50%) rotate(15deg); /* Add a tilt */
    }
  }
</style>
